/*****************************************************************************
    colorList -- the colours as a poured list (Tony and Clay, 2026-11-22, first draft;
    the final form takes shape by rinse and repeat). Definitions only. Fire it with
    Start(); show(colorList);  NOT RUNNABLE YET: pour:= and each are not built (the
    pour dispatch). Until then tester draws the same shape by hand (colorListHand).
    The form names no colour and no font of its own: only placeholders, resolved
    through the look (IncantForms/Controls/styles).
*****************************************************************************/
/*  The words for each colour, keyed by the colour's own name, as dESCRIPTIONs is keyed
    by field name. The form reads them with a registry-qualified insert,
    {cOLOrdESCRIPTIONs.each}, so nothing else on the search list can answer.
    A colour with no entry here shows nothing in its third cell.
    Defined with only Grokking searched: with cOLOr on the list, black="..." would reopen cOLOr's black
    and overwrite its value (measured by Clod, 2026-11-22, the pour stroke). The search line after puts the colours back.  */
search reset stack Grokking;
registry(cOLOrdESCRIPTIONs);
define
    black="the darkest; the fallback text and border colour";
    blue="a strong mid blue";
    darkBrown="a deep brown";
    darkerGray="a cool mid grey";
    gray="a light grey";
    green="a strong green";
    lightBlue="a very pale blue";
    lightGreen="a soft green; the default look's tab fill";
    paleGray="the palest grey";
    radialGreen="the same value as lightGreen, kept under its old name";
    red="a strong red; the default look's accent";
    saberBrown="a sand brown";
    wall="a pale yellow; the old forms' page colour";
    white="white; the default look's page fill";
    ;
search cOLOr fONTs sTYLEs;
register(FORMs);
/*  One template row (clRow: down on the field, across and the height on its one row, the G3 grid rule), repeated once per cOLOr entry in order (pour:=, on a down="*" field).
    each names the entry the copy is for: {each.taG} prints its name, {each} its value,
    fill:=each paints it. color:=contrast picks black or white text from the field's own
    fill. All three are new (the pour dispatch); everything else is built.  */
define
    colorList window x=0 y=0 width=490 height=792 down fill:=pageFill font:=bodyFont title="Colors"
        clTitle="Colors" text height=40 font:=headingFont align=center valign=center bottomBorder;
        clRows down="*" pour:=cOLOr
            clRow across height=24
                clName="{each.taG}" width=30% valign=center;
                clSwatch="{each}" width=25% fill:=each color:=contrast align=center valign=center;
                clWhat="{cOLOrdESCRIPTIONs.each}" valign=center;
    ;
bail();

